{"duration_api_ms":279075,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"c1ead64e-50b4-40f4-a63b-9924fab1d92b","total_cost_usd":0.312472,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12582,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":26214,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":20332},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12582,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":26214,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12582,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12582},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":26214,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":12582,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.312472,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":20332,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"observation\":\"Both objectives are minimised and the hypervolume is dominated by bondline temperature: reference 450 K, range 150 K. The two front points are C-ebc970ec4c08 (326k W/m2, 398.9 K) and C-1d363bb5fb96 (303k W/m2, 418.0 K). Heat flux is already about 12% of its reference, so lowering temperature at roughly 300-330k W/m2 gains the most hypervolume. Three constraints bind. (1) max_g is limited to 12 and depends almost only on flight_path_angle and weakly on D, about 1.64 g per deg. (2) Heatshield mass margin shrinks about 0.55 per metre of D, reaching zero near D~3.38 for cone 70. (3) Geometry validity: the failure messages are consistent with b*cos(theta) + 0.1*(1-cos(theta)) <= 0.5, which I fitted from the three failure messages that reported cone length (C-89104d06b31b, C-9a8f6b34e7d6, C-2e989122c857). This caps bluntness at about 1.27 for cone 70. Every proposal keeps b <= 1.25 at cone 70. Larger D, bluntness around 1.0-1.25, cone 70 and gamma near -3.5 to -3.6 look best. Shallower gamma at large D should extend the low-heat-flux end of the front.\",\"evidence\":[\"C-1d363bb5fb96, C-79b4f21cd368 and C-ffcd43d3a722 (D3.1, b1.0, cone 66) give T = 418.0, 401.0, 397.9 K at gamma -2.2, -3.5, -3.8. Steeper entry lowers temperature but max_g goes 9.87, 11.73, 12.22, so gamma near -3.6 is the g limit.\",\"C-79b4f21cd368 and C-7f9191564183 differ only in cone angle (66 vs 70) and have identical T, HF and g. Cone angle affects only mass margin (0.1527 vs 0.1568) and geometry validity.\",\"D scaling at gamma -3.5: D2.5 (C-db21b2a40acf) gives 466k W/m2 and 415 K; D3.1 gives 341k and 401 K; D3.25 (C-ebc970ec4c08) gives 326k and 398.9 K. Larger D is better for both objectives until the mass margin runs out (0.071 at D3.25).\",\"Bluntness: C-9abcecb64f83 (D3.0, b0.9) gives 362.9k W/m2 and 405.1 K; C-54385b92fe47 (D3.0, b0.5) gives 438.8k and 412.9 K. C-04b40d986adf (D2.9, b1.15, cone 70) matches C-9abcecb64f83 even at smaller D. So b helps but with diminishing returns.\",\"Mass margin vs D at cone 66-70: 0.449 at D2.5, 0.313 at D2.8, 0.2003 at D3.0, 0.1527 at D3.1, 0.0711 at D3.25. C-f97dae207371 (cone 37.6) has -0.127 while C-d886270d6bf7 (cone 65, same D and b) has +0.079, so high cone angles are lighter.\",\"Geometry failures at small cone angle relative to b: C-f7129c4fe153, C-9a8f6b34e7d6, C-2e989122c857. Feasible: C-04b40d986adf (b1.15, cone 70) and C-b2f6fa6659c9. This supports the b*cos(theta) rule, which puts the bluntness limit at cone 70 near 1.27.\"],\"mechanism\":\"Peak stagnation heat flux scales roughly as D^-1.36 and weakly with bluntness (b^-0.2 to -0.3). It depends weakly on gamma, roughly sin(gamma)^0.25. Bondline temperature follows heat load, so it falls with D, b and steeper entry. Peak g depends mainly on gamma, so it caps steepness at about -3.6. Cone 70 gives the lightest shield and the largest allowed b, which lets D rise to about 3.3-3.35 before mass fraction binds. Shallower gamma at large D lowers peak heat flux at the cost of temperature, which spreads the front toward the low-heat-flux end.\",\"uncertainty\":\"All exponents and offsets are extrapolated from 19 feasible points. I have no direct data for D>3.25, b>1.15, or the true shape of temperature vs gamma at shallow angles. The mass-fraction limit at D~3.35-3.45 is extrapolated, as is the possibility that the b benefit reverses (for example from radiative heating). The geometry rule is a fit and may be off near b~1.25 at cone 70. These predictions rely on prior physical knowledge as much as on the data.\",\"proposals\":[{\"parent_id\":\"C-ebc970ec4c08\",\"rationale\":\"Slightly larger D and more bluntness at the g limit to push temperature below 398.9 K.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.3,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.55},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":314000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":397.3,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests whether D3.3 keeps the mass margin positive while improving both objectives.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-ebc970ec4c08\",\"rationale\":\"Probe the mass-fraction edge at D3.35 with b1.0 at gamma -3.5.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.35,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.0},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":308000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":397.5,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Locates the mass limit while offering a likely front point.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-ebc970ec4c08\",\"rationale\":\"Raise bluntness to 1.2 at D3.3, cone 70 (geometry valid, b<=1.27).\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.3,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.2},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":305000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":397.3,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Separates the b effect from the D effect in the large-D region.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-ebc970ec4c08\",\"rationale\":\"Near-maximum bluntness 1.25 (valid at cone 70) with a steeper gamma just inside the g limit.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.3,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.25,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.58},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":303000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":396.5,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests the geometry boundary and whether the bluntness benefit continues; predicted g is about 11.94.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-ebc970ec4c08\",\"rationale\":\"Keep D3.25 (known mass margin 0.071) and raise b and steepness.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"bluntness_ratio\":1.1,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.6},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":315000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":397.3,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Low-risk improvement that isolates the b and gamma effects at a known D.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-ebc970ec4c08\",\"rationale\":\"Probe the mass limit beyond D3.4 with high b.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.45,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.25,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.4},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":285000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":396.5,\"feasible\":false},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Defines the D upper bound for the remaining rounds; a mass-fraction violation is expected.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-ebc970ec4c08\",\"rationale\":\"Change D only, keeping b0.9 and gamma -3.5, to isolate the D effect.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.3},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":320000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":398.2,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Cleanly measures the D gradient near the mass limit.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-ebc970ec4c08\",\"rationale\":\"D3.35 with b1.2 at gamma -3.55 to combine all favourable levers.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.35,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.2,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.55},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":302000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":396.8,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Best-guess lowest-temperature feasible design; predicted g about 11.91.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-1d363bb5fb96\",\"rationale\":\"Mid-front point: larger D, cone 70, b1.2 at gamma -3.0.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.3,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.2,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.0},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":296000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":405.0,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Fills the trade-off between the two current front points.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-1d363bb5fb96\",\"rationale\":\"Same design with gamma -2.5 for front coverage.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.3,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.2,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":285000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":409.5,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Samples the heat-flux vs temperature slope at moderate gamma.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-1d363bb5fb96\",\"rationale\":\"Improve the low-heat-flux end at gamma -2.2 via larger D and b.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.3,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.2,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":275000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":415.5,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Direct improvement over C-1d363bb5fb96 in both objectives.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-1d363bb5fb96\",\"rationale\":\"Shallower gamma -1.8 for lower heat flux at large D.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.3,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.2,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.8},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":257000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":422.0,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Extends the front toward low heat flux; temperature stays well below the 450 K limit.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-1d363bb5fb96\",\"rationale\":\"Extreme shallow entry gamma -1.55 with max valid bluntness for a low-heat-flux extreme.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.3,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.25,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.55},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":243000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":426.0,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests how far heat flux can fall before temperature approaches its limit; the shallow-gamma trend is extrapolated.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-ebc970ec4c08\",\"rationale\":\"D3.3, b1.1 with a slightly shallower gamma of -3.3.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.3,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.1,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.3},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":302000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":399.6,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Adds coverage between the steepest and moderate points at high D.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-ebc970ec4c08\",\"rationale\":\"D3.2 with b1.25 and steep gamma, retaining more mass margin.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.2,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.25,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.6},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":314000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":398.4,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests the bluntness benefit at a mass-safe diameter.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-ebc970ec4c08\",\"rationale\":\"D3.35, b1.2 at gamma -3.2 for front coverage.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.35,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.2,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.2},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":293000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":401.0,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"A low-heat-flux point near 400 K that may dominate C-1d363bb5fb96.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-ebc970ec4c08\",\"rationale\":\"D3.35, b1.2 at gamma -2.8.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.35,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.2,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.8},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":284000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":405.5,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Fills the mid-front region between 400 K and 415 K.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-1d363bb5fb96\",\"rationale\":\"D3.3, b1.1 at gamma -2.0 to space the front.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.3,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.1,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.0},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":270000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":418.5,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Adds a point at a distinct gamma to define the shallow-side front shape.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-ebc970ec4c08\",\"rationale\":\"D3.38 with b1.25, close to the estimated mass edge.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.38,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.25},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":290000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":396.5,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Mass margin is predicted to be about zero, so this tests the boundary; high potential reward.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-ebc970ec4c08\",\"rationale\":\"D3.25, b1.25 at gamma -2.3 for another mid-front point.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"bluntness_ratio\":1.25,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.3},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":274000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":414.0,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Uses the known-safe D3.25 mass margin to test high bluntness at shallow gamma.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0}]}","ttft_ms":227766,"type":"result","duration_ms":279106,"uuid":"0ae5f6ca-7637-42be-979d-731b5ad95fc2","ttft_stream_ms":1685,"time_to_request_ms":35,"first_content_frame_ms":1685,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
